led The Geology Department at San José State University is pleased to announce a search for an Assistant Professor in Geophysics beginning in August 2026. We are seeking a geophysicist with research interests and expertise in topics including seismology, tectonics, geodynamics, and geophysical exploration. Teaching duties will include undergraduate and graduate courses in geophysics. Personnel and Projects Specialist San José September 01, 2026 Open Until Filled The Personnel and Projects Specialist coordinates complex personnel processes, maintains and analyzes confidential personnel and organizational information, supports division-wide projects and change initiatives, and serves as a liaison among People and Culture, Directors of Resources and Operations (DROs), managers, and unit analysts. Department Analyst San José September 01, 2026 Open Until Filled The College of Humanities and the Arts is seeking a Department Analyst to support the Department of Film and Theatre. Conference and Administrative Services Coordinator San José September 01, 2026 Open Until Filled Reporting to the Senior Director, University Housing, and receiving work lead direction from the Conferences and Administrative Services Specialist, the Conference and Administrative Services Coordinator to perform duties under general supervision and works independently to assist with administering the Conference Housing Program, a comprehensive program providing summer and academic year student, conference group and guest housing services for approximately 5,000 to 7,500 individuals annually. The Conference and Administrative Services Coordinator oversees housing mailroom locations on and off campus, which includes student supervision, customer and guest support for residents and parents. Senior Director, Energy & Utilities San José August 27, 2026 Open Until Filled San José State University is seeking an accomplished Senior Director of Energy and Utilities to lead critical campus infrastructure, energy strategy, and sustainability initiatives. Join us in strengthening campus resiliency through regulatory compliance, emergency preparedness, resource stewardship, service excellence, and advancement of the university’s carbon neutrality goals. SWANA Initiatives Specialist San José August 26, 2026 Open Until Filled Reporting to the Senior Director, Identity Based Retention Centers and receiving work lead direction under the general supervision from the Program Director for the Mosaic Cross Cultural Center, the SWANA Initiatives Specialist supports the development, coordination, implementation, and assessment of culturally relevant student success programs and workshops that center and celebrate the experiences, identities, and contributions of students of Southwest Asian and North African (SWANA) descent.  The role prioritizes creating inclusive, identity-affirming spaces and initiatives that promote engagement, leadership development, and holistic student success within the SWANA student community. Student Support Specialist (TEMP) San José August 26, 2026 Open Until Filled Reporting directly to the Senior Director of Identity-Based Retention Centers, the Student Support Specialist supports San José State University’s commitment to student success and equity by advancing retention and persistence efforts under the CSU Advancing Student Achievement Program (ASAP) grant. The position is responsible for providing culturally responsive services that enhance the educational experiences and promote the success of low-income, first-generation, and underserved Asian, Native Hawaiian, and Pacific Islander (AANHPI) students, as well as other underrepresented student populations. Assistant Professor, Computer Engineering San José August 25, 2026 Open Until Filled The Computer Engineering Department at San José State University is pleased to announce a search for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning in January or August 2027. Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemical and Materials Engineering San José August 25, 2026 Open Until Filled The Department of Chemical and Materials Engineering at San José State University is pleased to announce a search for one tenured/tenure-track position in the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor in Materials Engineering beginning in August 2026. Director of Development, Technology Sector San José August 25, 2026 Open Until Filled The Director develops relationships with technology executives, founders, investors, entrepreneurs, and industry leaders whose interests may span multiple areas of the university. The Director is responsible for identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding alumni, parents, friends, and other prospective donors with professional or philanthropic interests in technology, information systems, entrepreneurship, innovation, and related fields. Box Office Supervisor San José August 24, 2026 Open Until Filled The Hammer Theatre is seeking a Box Office Supervisor to join the team! This position oversees box office operations, including ticketing, customer service, financial reporting, event support, and the hiring, training, and scheduling of student assistants. Associate Director, Central Plant & Energy Services San José August 24, 2026 Open Until Filled Join San José State University as the Associate Director, Central Plant & Energy Services and provide strategic leadership for safe, reliable, efficient, and sustainable campus utility operations and energy services. Laborer San José August 24, 2026 Open Until Filled Under supervision of the Director for Facilities Operations, the Laborer primarily performs general unskilled manual labor.  This includes a variety of general repair work and preventive maintenance that does not require journey-level skills, assisting with moving/relocation scheduled work requests, uses powered or non-powered cleaning and materials handling equipment and delivery trucks. Performs other tasks such as the collection, segregation and recycling of various materials, the set up and break down of tables, chairs and canopies, the movement of furniture within/to/from an office, assists with relocation needs due to repairs and the set up and break down for annual Admitted Spartan Day and Opening Days. Operations & Supply Chain Management Lecturer Pool San José August 21, 2026 Open Until Filled The Department of Operations and Supply Chain Management prepares students to become skilled professionals and innovative leaders in operations and supply chain management. The department offers one concentration in Operations and Supply Chain Management, providing students with current knowledge, practical experience, and opportunities to develop essential analytical, technical, and leadership skills. The concentration prepares graduates to manage operations, logistics, sourcing, quality, and supply chain activities in complex global business environments. (https://www.sjsu.edu/oscm/) Associate Dean for Academic Programs, Student Success & Assessment San José August 20, 2026 Open Until Filled Join San José State University as the Associate Dean for Academic Programs, Student Success and Assessment and play a key leadership role in advancing academic excellence and student success. Department Analyst San José August 20, 2026 Open Until Filled Reporting to the Director of Resources and Operations and receiving work lead direction from the Department chair, this position is responsible for the day-to-day operations and activities of the department. This incumbent works with limited supervision to provide various moderately complex analyst support to the Department Chair, faculty, and students of the Communicative Disorders & Sciences Department. Facilities Control Specialist San José August 19, 2026 Open Until Filled Reporting to the Associate Director, Building Infrastructure Trades, The Facilities Control Specialist is responsible for the installation, maintenance, adjustment and repair of electric, electronic, pneumatic and digitally controlled building automation systems, which manage the most complex HVAC and refrigeration systems. Associate Director, Athletic Fields San José August 19, 2026 Open Until Filled The Associate Director, Athletic Fields provides strategic leadership and oversight of South Campus grounds operations in support of Division I Athletics and campus landscape services. This role manages daily operations, staff, budgets, and sustainability initiatives to ensure high-quality, compliant, and environmentally responsible grounds maintenance with broad organizational impact. More Jobs 206 Current opportunities Position Location Open Date Close Date Faculty Employment Specialist San José September 04, 2026 Open Until Filled Join our Faculty Services team and help shape the faculty employment experience at the University. As a Faculty Employment Specialist, you’ll play a critical role in supporting faculty and Academic Student Employee appointments and hiring while partnering across colleges and departments to advance academic excellence, institutional priorities, and a strong university community. Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Chemistry San José September 01, 2026 Open Until Filled The Department of Chemistry at San José State University is pleased to announce a search for a tenure track assistant professor position in chemistry beginning in August 2027. Excellence in research and teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate level is expected. The candidate will be teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Analytical and/or Physical chemistry. Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Geology - Geophysicist San José September 01, 2026 Open Until Filled The Geology Department at San José State University is pleased to announce a search for an Assistant Professor in Geophysics beginning in August 2026. We are seeking a geophysicist with research interests and expertise in topics including seismology, tectonics, geodynamics, an